C compiler for Minix on the rosco_m68k
======================================

The chain, as on the old Minix-ST with c68 and the Sozobon tools:

	cpp -> c68 (ACK assembler syntax, 16 bit int) -> jas -> ld -> a.out

	c68/		the C compiler
	cpp/		the C preprocessor (not built yet)
	sozobon/	assembler (jas), linker (ld), archiver (tools/ar.c)
	Makefile	builds the host versions into host/

`make` here builds host/c68, host/jas, host/ld and host/ar.  Example:

	host/c68 -int=16 x.c x.s	# ACK syntax
	host/jas -o x.o x.s
	host/ar r lib.a x.o
	host/ld -o prog =8192 crt0.o main.o lib.a	# =N: stack bytes

ld writes a Minix executable (32 byte header with A_M68K, then text, data
and the relocation in GEMDOS format), as src/rosco/tools/mkminix.py does
for the gcc-built programs.

Sources and licenses
--------------------

c68/ and cpp/: from xtc68, https://codeberg.org/stronnag/xtc68 (formerly
github.com/stronnag/xtc68), commit 206699274d70 (2026-06-28), src/c68,
src/cpp and src/include/xtc68.h, unchanged.  xtc68 is the c68 4.5 code
base (27 Feb 99) made to build on modern hosts; LICENSE.xtc68 (MIT) covers
the xtc68 changes.

  c68: Copyright 1989-1991 Christoph van Wuellen, later Dave and Keith
  Walker and others.  "This compiler may be redistributed as long there is
  no commercial interest.  The compiler must not be redistributed without
  its full sources."  Hence the whole src/c68 directory, also the code
  generators for other processors.

  cpp: GNU cccp (the GNU C preprocessor of gcc 1.x), GNU General Public
  License, see the notices in cpp/cccp.c and cpp/cexp.c.

sozobon/: the Sozobon C compiler 2.0 sources, "sozobon 2.0 (Original).zip"
from https://sourceforge.net/projects/sozobon ("Source code"): jas, ld,
tools and readme.src.  Copyright 1988-1991 Sozobon, Limited (Joseph M
Treat, Johann Ruegg, Tony Andrews): free use and redistribution, no charge
other than for reproduction, modified versions must be clearly marked.

  MODIFIED for this port:
  - all files: DOS line ends (CR LF) converted to LF;
  - sozobon/host32.h (new): for the host build on an LP64 system, force
    included: the system headers first, then "#define long int" (the
    sources write longs to the object and executable files and assume 32
    bits), and link, strnlen, bcopy renamed (they clash with the host C
    library);
  - ld/utls.c, tools/ar.c: K&R "long lseek();" declarations removed
    (lseek() comes from <unistd.h> with its off_t argument);
  - ld/pass2.c: MMAGIC writes a_cpu 0x0B (A_M68K) instead of 0x04 (i8086,
    what the old Minix-ST tools used; MM accepts both).
  The modified files carry a MODIFIED note and "rosco:" comments.

jas must be built with -DMINIX for the ACK syntax (.sect, ! comments,
input compatible with the Minix ACK assembler), ld with -DMINIX for the
Minix output.

Support routines
----------------

c68 calls .Xldiv, .Xlrem, .Xlmul, the unsigned .Xul* and the assigning
.Xas* forms for long arithmetic: operands on the stack (4(sp) the left
operand or a pointer to it, 8(sp) the right one), the routine pops them
and returns the result in d0.  They go into the c68 library.
